From 2e030f3de8dd42f0e638928c537c55133511ea4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:23:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf][Qwen4Exp] Stage pure-prefill PLE rows from
 host-computed ids

The host_file_gather staging path syncs the worker's whole stream every
step to bring ngram ids back from the GPU before preadv'ing rows. Under
PP=4 with concurrent prefills that CPU-side backlog wait collapses the
RPC pipeline: batch prefill bimodally flips between ~275 s and ~370 s
runs, while pinned-UVA holds a steady ~350. Moving the gather to a
background thread alone does not fix it: decode ids depend on the
previous step's sampled token, so the GPU round-trip stays on the
critical path, and a step that reads the single staging buffer before
its own barrier lands serves stale rows.

Pure-prefill steps need no GPU round-trip at all. Every scheduled token
is a prompt token, and the full prompt already reaches the worker in
NewRequestData.prefill_token_ids. Mirror it per request in host memory;
for batches that are prefill-only, draft-free, and covered by the
mirror, compute ngram ids on the CPU and hand the gather thread pinned
ids directly. The thread preadvs rows while the previous forward is in
flight, then orders the H2D behind a submit-time event on the main
stream and records a barrier; the worker places that barrier before
this step's forward, so the staging write can neither race the previous
read nor this one. The worker only waits the thread's enqueue, bounded
by the gather itself and never by the GPU backlog.

Decode, mixed, draft, and mirror-uncovered steps keep the lockstep path
unchanged. The fast path is opt-in (VLLM_PLE_GATHER_PIPELINE=1, default
0): on the 4x170HX PP=4 testbed it measured slower than lockstep (100/4
at 389-414 s vs 276-380, cold 1M +2.5 s) because the gather wait it
hides was never the batch bottleneck, while the worker-side id compute
taxes every prefill step. Correctness gates passed: logprob A/B inside
the noise floor, needles exit 0, decode-window acceptance 4.99.
